@@ -40,6 +40,13 @@ Cards automatically "postpone" (move to "not now") after inactivity:
 - Prevents endless todo lists from accumulating
 - Configurable via Account/Board settings
 
+### Stalled Cards
+
+Cards that get a burst of attention and then go cold are flagged (all in `Card::Stallable`):
+- A burst is three or more comments from at least two people landing within a third of the board's auto-close period; being assigned or reopened also bursts a card
+- The burst is stamped on `cards.burst_at`, and any activity on the card wipes it, so a card has to earn a new burst to stall again
+- Two weeks of silence after a burst stalls a card: it shows the card bubble ("Stalled for N days") and is listed with `indexed_by=stalled`
+
 ### UUID Primary Keys
 
 All tables use UUIDs (UUIDv7 format, base36-encoded as 25-char strings):
